dified residue","start":407,"end":407,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":424,"end":424,"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine"},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":445,"end":445,"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine"},{"type":"Disulfide bond","start":462,"end":495,"description":""},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":541,"end":541,"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine"},{"type":"Disulfide bond","start":551,"end":551,"description":"Interchain"},{"type":"Domain","start":624,"end":726,"description":"Fibronectin type-III 1"},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":633,"end":633,"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine"},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":651,"end":651,"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine"},{"type":"Disulfide bond","start":674,"end":899,"description":""},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":698,"end":698,"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine"},{"type":"Region","start":733,"end":741,"description":"Insulin-binding"},{"type":"Domain","start":757,"end":842,"description":"Fibronectin type-III 2"},{"type":"Topological domain","start":763,"end":956,"description":"Extracellular"},{"type":"Chain","start":763,"end":1382,"description":"Insulin receptor subunit beta"},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":769,"end":769,"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine"},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":782,"end":782,"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine"},{"type":"Disulfide bond","start":825,"end":834,"description":""},{"type":"Domain","start":853,"end":947,"description":"Fibronectin type-III 3"},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":920,"end":920,"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine"},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":933,"end":933,"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine"},{"type":"Transmembrane","start":957,"end":979,"description":"Helical"},{"type":"Topological domain","start":980,"end":1382,"description":"Cytoplasmic"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":992,"end":992,"description":"Phosphotyrosine; by autocatalysis"},{"type":"Region","start":999,"end":999,"description":"Important for interaction with IRS1, SHC1 and STAT5B"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":999,"end":999,"description":"Phosphotyrosine; by autocatalysis"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1011,"end":1011,"description":"Phosphotyrosine; by autocatalysis"},{"type":"Domain","start":1023,"end":1298,"description":"Protein kinase"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1033,"end":1033,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1057,"end":1057,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":1079,"end":1079,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1083,"end":1083,"description":"S-nitrosocysteine"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1104,"end":1110,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Active site","start":1159,"end":1159,"description":"Proton donor/acceptor"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1163,"end":1164,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1177,"end":1177,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1185,"end":1185,"description":"Phosphotyrosine; by autocatalysis"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1189,"end":1189,"description":"Phosphotyrosine; by autocatalysis"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1190,"end":1190,"description":"Phosphotyrosine; by autocatalysis"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1355,"end":1355,"description":"Phosphotyrosine; by autocatalysis"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1361,"end":1361,"description":"Phosphotyrosine; by autocatalysis"},{"type":"Region","start":1361,"end":1364,"description":"PIK3R1-binding"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Tetramer of 2 alpha and 2 beta chains linked by disulfide bonds. The alpha chains carry the insulin-binding regions, while the beta chains carry the kinase domain. Forms a hybrid receptor with IGF1R, the hybrid is a tetramer consisting of 1 alpha chain and 1 beta chain of INSR and 1 alpha chain and 1 beta chain of IGF1R. Interacts with SORBS1 but dissociates from it following insulin stimulation. Binds SH2B2. Activated form of INSR interacts (via Tyr-999) with the PTB/PID domains of IRS1 and SHC1. The sequences surrounding the phosphorylated NPXY motif contribute differentially to either IRS1 or SHC1 recognition. Interacts (via tyrosines in the C-terminus) with IRS2 (via PTB domain and 591-786 AA); the 591-786 would be the primary anchor of IRS2 to INSR while the PTB domain would have a stabilizing action on the interaction with INSR. Interacts with the SH2 domains of the 85 kDa regulatory subunit of PI3K (PIK3R1) in vitro, when autophosphorylated on tyrosine residues. Interacts with SOCS7. Interacts (via the phosphorylated Tyr-999), with SOCS3. Interacts (via the phosphorylated Tyr-1185, Tyr-1189, Tyr-1190) with SOCS1. Interacts with CAV2 (tyrosine-phosphorylated form); the interaction is increased with 'Tyr-27'phosphorylation of CAV2 (By similarity). Interacts with ARRB2 (By similarity). Interacts with GRB10; this interaction blocks the association between IRS1/IRS2 and INSR, significantly reduces insulin-stimulated tyrosine phosphorylation of IRS1 and IRS2 and thus decreases insulin signaling. Interacts with GRB7. Interacts with PDPK1. Interacts (via Tyr-1190) with GRB14 (via BPS domain); this interaction protects the tyrosines in the activation loop from dephosphorylation, but promotes dephosphorylation of Tyr-999, this results in decreased interaction with, and phosphorylation of, IRS1. Interacts (via subunit alpha) with ENPP1 (via 485-599 AA); this interaction blocks autophosphorylation. Interacts with PTPRE; this interaction is dependent of Tyr-1185, Tyr-1189 and Tyr-1190 of the INSR. Interacts with STAT5B (via SH2 domain). Interacts with PTPRF. Interacts with ATIC; ATIC together with PRKAA2/AMPK2 and HACD3/PTPLAD1 is proposed to be part of a signaling netwok regulating INSR autophosphorylation and endocytosis (By similarity). Interacts with the cone snail venom insulin Con-Ins G1 (PubMed:27617429). Interacts with the insulin receptor SORL1; this interaction strongly increases its surface exposure, hence strengthens insulin signal reception (PubMed:27322061). Interacts (tyrosine phosphorylated) with CCDC88A/GIV (via SH2-like region); binding requires autophosphorylation of the INSR C-terminal region (PubMed:25187647). Interacts with GNAI3; the interaction is probably mediated by CCDC88A/GIV (PubMed:25187647). Interacts with LMBRD1 (By similarity). Interacts (in response to insulin stimulation) with NCK1; this interaction may recruit PTPN1 to mediate INSR dephosphorylation (PubMed:21707536). Interacts with CD248; this interaction diminishes INSR autophosphorylation (By similarity)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"P06213-2","name":"Short","synonyms":["HIR-A"],"notes":[],"length":1370,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000341500.9"],"refseq":["NM_001079817.3"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001073285.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,744],[745,757,626]],"edits":[{"start":745,"end":756,"original":"KTSSGTGAEDPR","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":12,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":0,"foldedMissing":0,"features":[[1,12,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-P06213-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P06213-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":78.4,"plddt":[[50,1],[0,26],[50,2],[70,1],[50,1],[70,2],[90,3],[70,1],[90,3],[70,7],[90,16],[70,8],[90,2],[70,2],[90,25],[70,1],[90,9],[70,8],[90,22],[70,2],[90,7],[70,1],[90,5],[70,1],[90,8],[70,7],[90,1],[70,2],[90,2],[70,9],[90,1],[70,2],[50,6],[70,7],[50,1],[70,4],[90,14],[70,1],[90,8],[70,1],[90,45],[70,2],[90,10],[70,6],[50,5],[0,1],[50,3],[70,2],[90,8],[70,10],[50,1],[70,3],[90,3],[70,15],[90,4],[70,8],[90,1],[70,2],[90,11],[70,2],[50,4],[70,7],[90,17],[70,4],[90,28],[70,2],[90,1],[70,2],[90,2],[70,4],[90,15],[70,2],[90,3],[70,1],[90,16],[70,2],[90,3],[70,8],[50,1],[70,1],[50,1],[70,3],[90,17],[70,12],[90,9],[70,2],[90,1],[70,4],[50,6],[0,3],[50,2]